  "headline": "Nasdaq-100 holds fresh-record calm into the Asia handover -- VIX near a seven-month low (~14.5-14.7), 10Y ~4.65% -- as Applied Materials' after-hours slide holds near -5% on a free-cash-flow miss, with no confirmed broad semiconductor-equipment follow-through ahead of Friday's Retail Sales/UMich cluster.",
  "body": "Roughly three hours past the 20:00 UTC cash close, conditions remain calm and largely unchanged from the prior run. The S&P 500 finished at a fresh record 7,798.99 (+0.65%, its first close above 7,800) and the Nasdaq Composite gained 0.81% to 26,803.03 on a flat July PPI print that undershot consensus. The VIX remains pinned near a seven-month low (~14.5-14.7), the 10-year Treasury yield holds around 4.65%, and WTI/Brent sit near their recent lows (~$81-82 / $87.07). Alpha Vantage's free-tier daily quota remains fully exhausted this run (a fresh attempt and one retry both returned rate_limit errors before any data was retrieved), so this assessment again relies entirely on cross-confirmed web research, and Confidence is held at a similar medium-low level to reflect that gap. Applied Materials' after-hours reaction has held steady near -5.24% (to about $506.51) despite record Q3 revenue/EPS and 2026 equipment-growth guidance raised above 30%, as investors focus on a roughly 80% collapse in free cash flow to about $210 million against record revenue and the stock's elevated near-50x earnings multiple. Nearly three hours after the print, no confirmed broad Nasdaq-100, NQ-futures, or semiconductor-equipment-peer (Lam Research, KLA) follow-through has been identified in current search results, so this remains a contained single-name reaction and Tail holds low at 14%. Stress eases slightly further to 35% as the AMAT move continues to look contained and cross-asset signals (VIX, yields, oil) stay benign, though the unresolved Iran/Hormuz standoff (Washington and Tehran both holding their positions, Israel continuing operations in southern Lebanon) and Friday's Retail Sales/cash-open/UMich cluster keep Stress in the moderate band rather than dropping further. No new kinetic escalation or fresh market-transmission event has been identified in the geopolitical situation since the prior run.",
